# ARM 2 — BCL-xL BH3-groove senolytic candidate set (AGA-RX PATH C)
# Format: SMILES <tab> name <tab> rationale
# All SMILES verified via PubChem (CID in rationale). The LEAD is WEHI-539, the
# co-crystallized BCL-xL-selective BH3 mimetic in 3ZLR (X0B); re-docking it is the
# self-consistency / box-validation positive control. The set spans navitoclax-like
# fragments and BCL-xL-selective senolytics (A-1331852, A-1155463).
#
# A BH3-groove binder must (a) drop an acyl-sulfonamide / carboxylate to salt-bridge
# Arg139, and (b) fill the P2/P4 hydrophobic pockets (Phe97/Phe105/Phe146).

